# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 (a `for` over an array: one row a key, the index; each row a block of its own) and ruling FV (`@Flatten` adopts, after the tick its outer fires, the inner the outer then holds, and reads it from the next tick, owed): the click moves `$a` to 6 and gives each row's hold the row's `$v`; tick 2 reads it. Equal to the first run, on prismc-f4.
test each_row_flattens_its_own

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="go")
    1/[0]/0: Ui.Label(text="0: 5")
    1/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="1: 5")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1/[0]/0: Ui.Label(text="0: 6")
    1/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="1: 6")

tick 2
  changed:
    1/[0]/0: Ui.Label(text="0: 1")
    1/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="1: 2")
